{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 4184 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["E6", "D3"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage list shows sufentanil citrate injection as Current for both Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA, Inc. and Hospira, Inc., a Pfizer Company, with initial posting on 2022-05-03.",
      "cites": ["E17", "E18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hospira plant (FEI 1021343) that manufactures the NDC 00409338221 used at both Corvale sites was classified OAI after an inspection ending 2010-01-19, which was 4184 days before the 2022-05-03 posting.",
      "cites": ["E6", "E16", "E2", "E1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "That same plant received a Warning Letter on 2010-04-12 and additional OAI classifications after inspections ending 2011-06-17 and 2011-08-04.",
      "cites": ["E15", "E8", "E10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later inspections of the plant were classified VAI, most recently ending 2019-11-21, which was 894 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["E14", "D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "As of 2026-10-21 the shortage has been on FDA's list for 54 months.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 64 vials at 9 per day (7.1 days on hand) and Corvale General holds 134 vials at 8.3 per day (16.1 days on hand).",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top-ranked option is to transfer 17 vials of 50 ug/mL, 1 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which requires pharmacy director approval plus a DEA Form 222 or CSOS order for this Schedule II product.",
      "cites": ["D5"]
    }
  ]
}
